From 4906d91fd8b286df948cfafd54aa8841c03552a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 19:36:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 121/209] fix: an ambient light that was also asked to cast
 shadows could take the engine down

Ticking both "ambient" and "cast shadows" on one light crashed the engine. This is a stock
CRYENGINE 5.7 bug, not something the scene-referred work introduced, so the guard is not gated on
the switch.

The engine builds a shadow frustum and a one-pass shadow render view for any light carrying
DLF_CASTSHADOW_MAPS, ambient lights included, and parks the view in eUsageModeWriting on
pFr->pOnePassShadowView. The renderer's shadow-gen list walks only eDLT_DynamicLight and
eDLT_DeferredLight, never eDLT_DeferredAmbientLight, so that view is never consumed and never
switched to eUsageModeWritingDone. The next frame overwrites the pointer, the view is released
while still in Writing mode, and CRenderView::Clear() skips its three job-state waits (they sit
inside the WritingDone branch) before freeing the render items - assert in a Profile editor,
use-after-free on the render thread otherwise. It also leaked one shadow render view per frame and
made the shadow-pool packer free and re-allocate the light's block every frame.

Nothing ever read an ambient light's shadow map: the tiled stage guards the whole shadow block
with "not an ambient light", and the light never enters the shadow-mask frustum list. So no longer
asking for one cannot change a pixel on any path; it only removes the dangling view, the leak and
the wasted shadow geometry passes.

Under Scene Referred the same light is routed as a real fill light in the following commit, so it
is no longer a modulator and its Cast Shadows checkbox becomes meaningful - hence the test on the
3D engine's mirror of the switch rather than a blanket clear.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
---
 Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/LightEntity.cpp | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/LightEntity.cpp b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/LightEntity.cpp
index 712f4368..0f7c175f 100644
--- a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/LightEntity.cpp
+++ b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/LightEntity.cpp
@@ -1758,6 +1758,35 @@ void CLightEntity::UpdateCastShadowFlag(float fDistance, const SRenderingPassInf
 			m_light.m_Flags |= DLF_CASTSHADOW_MAPS;
 	}
 
+	// Ambient lights must never request a shadow map. This is a STOCK CRYENGINE 5.7 bug and the
+	// guard is deliberately NOT gated on the scene-referred switch, because the crash is stock.
+	//
+	// An ambient light is routed into eDLT_DeferredAmbientLight (RenderView.cpp:386), but the
+	// renderer's shadow-gen list walks only eDLT_DynamicLight and eDLT_DeferredLight
+	// (D3DShadows.cpp:60-87). So with DLF_CASTSHADOW_MAPS set we build the frustum here, and
+	// C3DEngine::PrepareShadowPasses takes a render view out of the pool, switches it to
+	// eUsageModeWriting and parks it on pFr->pOnePassShadowView (3DEngineRender.cpp:3800-3803) -
+	// and nothing ever consumes it or switches it to eUsageModeWritingDone. Next frame the same
+	// frustum overwrites the pointer, the view is released while still in eUsageModeWriting, and
+	// CRenderView::Clear() skips its three m_jobstate_*.Wait() calls (they sit inside
+	// `if (m_usageMode == eUsageModeWritingDone)`) before freeing the render items: assert in a
+	// Profile editor, use-after-free on the RenderThread otherwise. It also leaked one shadow
+	// render view per frame and thrashed the shadow pool packer, whose orphan test
+	// (D3DShadows.cpp:225-245) scans the deferred list only.
+	//
+	// Behaviour-preserving: an ambient light's shadow map has NO consumer. TiledLightVolumes.cpp
+	// guards the whole shadow block with `if (!ambientLight && ...)`, and the light never enters
+	// m_shadows.m_renderFrustums, so it gets no shadow-mask slice either. Not building it cannot
+	// change a pixel - it only stops the dangling view, the leak and the wasted geometry passes.
+	//
+	// On the scene-referred path an ambient light is re-routed to eDLT_DeferredLight as a real
+	// fill light (decisions/s8-ambient-lights.md part 2), so it is no longer a modulator and its
+	// Cast Shadows checkbox becomes meaningful - hence the switch test here rather than a blanket
+	// clear. Read through the 3DEngine-visible mirror of the renderer switch, which is the same
+	// value the routing in AddDeferredLight reads, so the two cannot disagree within a frame.
+	if ((m_light.m_Flags & DLF_AMBIENT) && !Get3DEngine()->IsSceneReferredConvention())
+		m_light.m_Flags &= ~DLF_CASTSHADOW_MAPS;
+
 #if defined(FEATURE_SVO_GI)
 	IRenderNode::EGIMode eVoxMode = GetGIMode();
 	if (eVoxMode == IRenderNode::eGM_DynamicVoxelization || (eVoxMode == IRenderNode::eGM_StaticVoxelization && !GetCVars()->e_svoTI_IntegrationMode && !(m_light.m_Flags & DLF_SUN)))
